\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Single-factor evaluation of the Maxwell--Kronecker projection over the full campaign range. Panels as in the main paper's single-factor compression test. In~(c) the retained energy fraction approaches the white-noise floor $r/I=1/16$ at $-20$~dB while the \emph  {uncompressed} subspace-leakage ratio $\sigma _{K+1}/\sigma _K$ reaches $0.99$ and the compressed one $0.81$; smaller is better, so this is the diagnostic form of delay-pole collapse, and the separation between the two curves is the margin the projection buys.}}{9}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:s_compression}{{8}{9}{}{}{}}
